sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as User Service<br/>(AccountPurgeScheduler)
    participant UDB as User DB
    participant C as SupplierBookmarkCleanupClient
    participant S as Supplier Service<br/>(PurgeController)
    participant SDB as Supplier DB
    participant G as API Gateway
    actor X as Caller outside the platform

    Note over P: scheduled purge run
    P->>UDB: read ids of accounts deleted before the cutoff<br/>(past the 30-day recovery window)
    alt no condemned accounts
        Note over P: nothing to clean, go to the account purge below
    else some condemned accounts
        P->>C: purgeBookmarks(ids)
        loop each batch of up to 500 ids
            C->>C: issueServiceToken() (role SERVICE, 1 minute)
            C->>S: POST /purge/bookmarks {userIds} + SERVICE token<br/>(direct, service to service over the compose network /<br/>cluster DNS, not via the gateway)
            Note over S: SecurityConfig: /purge/** requires the SERVICE role,<br/>a login token (USER, ADMIN, OWNER) gets 403, none gets 401
            S->>SDB: delete every bookmark of these user ids<br/>(idempotent, safe to repeat)
            S-->>C: 200 {deleted}
        end
    end
    alt every batch succeeded
        P->>UDB: in one transaction delete the accounts and their dependents,<br/>and write the user.purged events
    else a call failed or timed out (5 s connect, 15 s read)
        Note over P: error logged, no account deleted in this run, later batches not sent.<br/>Bookmarks of batches already answered stay deleted (each batch commits on its own),<br/>the rest stay, and the next run retries every account (the delete is idempotent)
    end

    X->>G: POST /api/supplier/purge/bookmarks
    G-->>X: 404 (the route is never proxied to the Supplier Service)
